1.1.evidence:
Second Part
Form and Mechanism of Services for Violence Against Women and Children Article 21 (1) In the context of providing protection services to women and children from acts of violence, the Regional Government establishes the Regional Technical Implementation Unit for the Protection of Women and Children (UPTD PPA), Integrated Referral Service System (SLRT), Task Force on Violence Against Women/Children (Tim KTP/A) in community health centers, Hospitals, schools, Islamic Boarding Schools, Women-Friendly and Child-Caring Villages (DRPPA).
(2) The Regional Government through UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1), functions to implement services:
a. Public complaints;
b. Victim outreach;
c. Case management;
d. Temporary shelter;
e. Mediation;
f. Victim assistance; and
g. Victim repatriation.
(3) Further provisions regarding the organization and working procedures of UPTD PPA as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by Regent Regulation. (4) To assist in the protection of women and children, the Regional Government establishes:
a. Task Force for the Prevention and Handling of Criminal Acts of Human Trafficking;
b. Task Force for the Prevention of Child Marriage;
c. Task Force for Child-Friendly Regency;
d. Regional Action Committee for the elimination of the worst forms of child labor or Worst Forms of Child Labor (BPTA); e. Regional Children's Forum (FAD);
f. Community-Based Integrated Child Protection (PATBM) PENA BISMA;
g. Domestic Violence Forum (KDRT);
h. Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children (Satgas PPA); i. Women-Friendly and Child-Caring Villages (DRPPA);
j. TIM KTP/A in Hospitals, Community health centers, schools, Islamic Boarding Schools.
(5) Further provisions regarding the establishment, duties, and functions of the task forces as referred to in paragraph (4) shall be stipulated by Regent Regulation.

